{
  "id": "u08-l02",
  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "Wake up, sleep, wash",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**At** a clock time = number + **-টা** + **-য়**:\n\n- **সাতটায়** (*shattay*) — at seven\n- **আটটায়** (*attay*) — at eight\n- **দশটায়** (*doshtay*) — at ten\n\nDon't mix it up with Unit 5: **দশটা বাজে** 'it's ten o'clock' has no **-য়**, but **আমি দশটায় ঘুমাই** 'I sleep *at* ten' does. To ask 'at what time?', add the same ending to **কয়টা**: **কয়টায়?** (*koytay*) — **আপনি কয়টায় ঘুমান?** 'What time do you go to bed?' Put the part of the day in front: **সকাল সাতটায়** 'at 7 a.m.', **রাত দশটায়** 'at 10 p.m.'\n\nTo wake up is **ঘুম থেকে ওঠা** — literally 'rise from sleep'. Watch the vowel: **আমি উঠি** but **আপনি ওঠেন**. Many common verbs swap o↔u or e↔i like this; more in Lesson 4.\n\n**গোসল করা** (*gosol kora*) is the everyday Bangladeshi word for bathing / showering. Kolkata (and many Hindu speakers) say *snan kora* instead.",
